1. Timer (drives sync)

Insert → Input → Timer. Put on Selected Video screen.

Duration: 300
Repeat: true
AutoStart: true
Visible: false
OnTimerEnd:
Set(varNow, Video1.Time)
2. Transcript gallery

Insert → Blank vertical gallery. Place right of video or below.

Items:

Sort(colCues, StartSec, Ascending)

Gallery props:

TemplateSize: 60
ShowScrollbar: true

Insert one Label inside the gallery template:

Text: ThisItem.CueText
AutoHeight: true
Width: gallery width minus 30
Size: 12
Fill (highlight active line):
If(
    ThisItem.StartSec <= varNow && ThisItem.EndSec >= varNow,
    RGBA(0, 120, 212, 0.15),
    Color.Transparent
)
3. Click-to-seek

Gallery OnSelect:

Set(varSeek, ThisItem.StartSec);
Set(varReset, true);
Set(varReset, false)

On Video1:

StartTime: varSeek
Reset: varReset



Two things to build. And one diagnostic — because "highlight stops after seeking" may be the highlight failing OR just being off-screen where you can't see it. Auto-scroll fixes both cases anyway.

1. Caption overlay on video

Insert → Text label. Place over bottom of video.

Text:

LookUp(colCues, StartSec <= varNow && EndSec >= varNow).CueText

Props:

X Video1.X + 20
Y Video1.Y + Video1.Height - 90
Width Video1.Width - 40
Height 60
Align Center
Size 14, Color White
Fill RGBA(0,0,0,0.6)
AutoHeight false

Right-click → Reorder → Bring to front. Else video covers it.

2. Auto-scroll — use a time window, not scrolling

Power Apps has no scroll-to-item function. Default doesn't reliably scroll. Real fix: stop showing all 199 cues. Show only cues near current time. Gallery never needs scrolling — active line is always in view.

Gallery Items:

Filter(
    colCues,
    EndSec >= varNow - 10 && StartSec <= varNow + 120
)

Shows ~10s behind, ~2min ahead. Rolls forward automatically as video plays. Seek anywhere → gallery jumps to that region instantly.

Tune: bigger 120 = more upcoming lines visible.

Click-to-seek still works unchanged.

3. Diagnostic — run this before assuming anything broke

Temp label, Text:

varNow & " | " & Video1.Time

Play → drag scrubber to 10:00 → watch both numbers.
